ake the back  seat for most of the film letting their  kids do the driving the Sully children  especially lowak Kiri and spider are  main characters in their own right and  they get plenty of wonderful character  development however many fans still miss  Jake and natiri some were especially  disappointed by natiri's limited screen  time and felt that natiri barely left a  dent in the sequel one person tweeted  she screams and fights but if her  dialogue reached 50 words I'd be  surprised still fans are at least glad  that natiri absolutely stole the scene  when she finally got a chance to shine  in the final battle  Jake and the teary weren't the only  characters who got the short end of the  stick the film has a gigantic cast with  two parents and five children plus  several more humans and met kaina  something was bound to slip through the  cracks on a Reddit Forum about the movie  One user complained that despite all the  buzz about Kate Winslet joining the cast  as Ronald her character wasn't given  much to do and while the story didn't  strictly need more scenes with Parker  Selfridge some fans actually missed his  presence one fan wrote a little bit  disappointed Selfridge was just a cameo  I thought a business suit type was a  nice yin yang Dynamic with the military  in the first movie  you see that yes sir no you didn't you  were looking at the monitor  even characters with a lot of screen  time like low OCT feel underdeveloped as  one fan noted the film could have been  even better if it spent a little longer  in lowatt growing to become friends with  his former bully perhaps the movie's  biggest sin is neglecting to develop  nateam since it's the last movie where  the character will appear as far as one  Reddit user was concerned I felt more  sadness about the depth of the whale on  her cap than about Jake's oldest son  dying  if something seemed a little bit off  while you were watching avatar the way  of water that's probably because you  noticed the movie's frame rate most  movies are shot at 24 frames per second  but the way of water was filmed at 48  frames per second as James Cameron  explained we're using High frame rate to  improve the 3D where we want to  heightened sense of presence such as  underwater or in some of the flying  scenes her shots of just people standing  around talking High frame rate works  against us because it creates a kind of  hyper realism in scenes that are more  mundane more normal viewers have said  that the frame rate made the film look  like a video game or a soap opera  meanwhile The Verge compared it to  watching quote a very expensive video  meant to be played on an array of  televisions in a Best Buy some fans were  comfortable with the 48 frames per  second but felt it was distracting when  the film switched back to 24 frames per  second one Reddit user pointed out that  the film would often toggle back and  forth between different frame rates  within a single scene they wrote that  sounds jarring that is because it was  one thing fans wanted to see more of was  the recombian soldiers recoms for short  supposedly kwara Rich Wayne Fleet and  the other recoms are a close-knit bunch  of soldiers who knew each other before  they were reborn in Navi bodies I know  you're all asking yourselves the same  question why so blue the viewers may  have a hard time buying that because  quarrich's buddies get zero character  development furthermore fans argue that  the recoms don't seem like much of a  threat Jake and natiri managed to take  them out almost single-handedly other  fans shared this sentiment with one  saying I love love loved the idea that  the RDA is using native fauna to slip  past AWA I was looking forward to seeing  them adapt more to their Navi bodies and  figure out the advantages but they just  kind of did what any six foot human  could have done while there's still a  chance that the recoms will get more  development in future movies some fans  may not want to wait that long  many fans watching avatar the way of  water were wondering why there was so  much English spoken as opposed to Navi  school begins Jake is considered one of  the navi and speaks her language so  shouldn't the movie have been entirely  in the Nabi language with English  subtitles the film does offer an  explanation for the switch even if fans  feel it's a contrived one Jake explains  that he has become accustomed to the  native tongue saying that it might as  well be English and that's when the  audio switches to English one Reddit  user wrote I understand why they did it  I just thought it was done without  finesse the subtlety of the linguistic  Switcheroo aside there's one particular  aspect of the dialogue and Avatar the  way of water that has elicited a strong  response from fans and not a good one  for some reason the teenage Navi  characters use slang words like cuz or  sick and the word bro is spoken several  times like all these aliens learned  English from 2000's era comedies wait  what about mine dude what does mine say  it's sweet what about mine dude what  does mine say  According to some Reddit users the slang  is cringe-worthy because it doesn't seem  in character for the navi one fan on  Reddit offered up an explanation  pointing out that the navi probably  aren't literally saying bro rather they  are using the navi equivalent which  Probably sounds less ridiculous and it  is translated for viewers just like  everything else the navi says as one  user said I just took it as when they're  speaking English it's Jake's  interpretation it makes sense Jake may  have many fine qualities but he's never  been a Wordsmith  oh here I am  doing science  mostly redditors wish the filmmakers had  taken the time to develop an equivalent  knobby word with a similar connotation  instead of relying on bro all the time  there's one thing fans and critics  mostly seem to agree on avatar the way  of water is a little too long certainly  the first avatar in Cameron's previous  filmography set a precedent remember the  double VHS set that held Titanic's a  Titanic three hour and 14 minute run  time I don't see what all the fuss is  about  it doesn't look any bigger than the  Mauritania you could be blase about  something's reals but not about Titanic  still many fans think Avatar the way of  water had no business being 3 hours and  12 minutes long one person wrote on  Twitter the ending runs a bit long and  the story doesn't justify it the runtime  has even alienated some moviegoers who  enjoy watching super long epics as one  redditor said mind you I regularly  watched The Lord of the Rings extended  editions I'm no stranger to long movies  but Avatar 2 really drags in response to  criticism about the movie's length James  Cameron told Empire magazine I don't  want anybody whining about length when  they sit and binge watch television for  eight hours  fans you can't please them all all the  time for every viewer who thought the  movie was too long it seems there's  someone else who thought it wasn't long  enough despite the film's lengthy run  time one Reddit user argues that the  movie's pacing often feels too fast  rather than too slow Cameron tries to  rush quickly through the First Act to  get Jake and his family to the Met  kainik Clan as quickly as possible  without giving the characters time to  breathe we barely get to see Jake  mourning what he's leaving behind for  one redditor the movie is actually  strongest when it takes its time they  wrote the downtime is what makes Avatar  so special in my opinion I come to these  movies for action and thrills yes but  also just to be immersed in an alien  world of course some fans think the  movie didn't need to be longer but still  wish that Cameron had cut a few subplots  so that the filmmakers could focus on  the most important storylines another  person took to Reddit to say it's  clearly a project of deep passion and  love and I respect that but I think that  passion also resulted in too many ideas  being crammed into a run time that was  already bursting at the seams in other  words the three-hour running time might  have been better spent on further  development for the main characters  while there is nothing in avatar The Way  of water as obvious as the infinity  stone scenes shoehorned into Avengers  Age of Ultron there are still several  plot threads introduced in this movie  that won't reach a satisfactory  conclusion until later in the Avatar  Saga for many fans this is infuriating  one person tweeted biggest issue feels  like a stepping stone for what's next  likewise a Reddit user was frustrated  that the valuable substance extracted by  humans from the brain to the Tolkien  that they brutally hunt down was  relevant for one scene and then  forgotten for the rest of the movie As  for the main characters it seems like  Kiri in particular won't get much payoff  until the sequels other fans wish the  film had explored why Kiri had a special  connection to the AWA and has seizures  underwater  heartbeat sound like mighty one redditor  concluded so much is left unresolved  debate for sequels I'm not invested in  yet not everyone felt this was a problem  as a redditor explained some very  Central and important characters are  basically only tagging along while some  other important characters get almost  all of the spotlight I'm sure these  characters will be given their moment in  future films so I will withhold final  judgment thankfully fans won't need to  wait another 13 years to see the payoff  Avatar 3 is projected to come out in  2024.  [Music]  foreign
 

